- Roland JD-800 (for icy, crystalline pad sweeps and digital vocal textures)
- Korg M1 (for bright, percussive dance-pop piano riffs)
- Akai S3000 Sampler (loaded with hydrophone field recordings of melting glacier caverns)
- Quartz crystal singing bowls (retuned to 432Hz and sustained infinitely)
- Alesis 3630 Compressor (cranked for hard-pumping dance-floor sidechaining)
- Shure SM58 (capturing belting, soulful 90s diva vocals)

For Fans Of: The KLF (Chill Out era), Saint Etienne, Enigma, William Orbit-era dance productions.

